# A connect the layer's poller wakes for nothing, whose failure lands between
# the two looks its loop takes, is told failed and never taken for a
# connection made (M-rebel-library step 87b). The loop read the pending error
# first and the writability second; a wake with nothing behind it, the
# poller's own for a slot given back and issued again, let the first look
# read no error while the connection was still being made, and a failure
# landing before the second look made the socket writable to `poll`, so the
# connect answered a connection its first send told RESET. Measured before
# the repair on Darwin and on Linux arm64, every run; the loop now looks at
# the writability first and reads the error after it, as at the deadline.
# The header beside this file is the layer itself with `getsockopt` wrapped,
# so it can send the wake and land the failure in the window; the first line
# is its control, the same far end failing with no wake. Each line prints 1
# where every step held, else the step that did not (the header says which).
# Built and not run on Windows, whose connect waits in slices and joins no
# waiter list (`tests/harness/platform_skips.hero`).
extern "the-platform-layer-connect-order.h" layer
    function connect_failed_while_it_waits() -> i64
    function connect_failed_between_two_looks_after_a_wake_for_nothing() -> i64

function main()
    print(f"a connect whose far end fails while it waits is told failed: {connect_failed_while_it_waits()}")
    print(
        f"a connect woken for nothing, failing between its two looks, is told failed: {connect_failed_between_two_looks_after_a_wake_for_nothing()}"
    )
